      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 Asia Oceania Association for the Study of Obesity. Published by Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
            "content": "The close connection between high blood FFA and insulin resistance (IR) in obese individuals is well-known. The purpose of this study was to identify whether the blood FFA increased in obese-IR animals."
          },
          {
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "Obese-IR animal models were established using high-fat diet (HFD) or HFD and streptozocin, and treated with drugs."
          },
          {
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "The serum FFA of obese-IR animals was not increased, even significantly lower than that of normal animals, and were not significantly decreased when insulin sensitivity and obesity-related indices were ameliorated after treatment."
          },
          {
            "Label": "CONCLUSION",
            "content": "The results suggest that blood FFA are unlikely the link between obesity and insulin resistance."
          }
        ]
      },
